# --- Running Metro (this `expo start`) on a machine reachable remotely ---
# e.g. the dedicated server from ../dedicated-server/, reached over
# Tailscale instead of plain LAN. Expo's own host-detection normally picks
# whatever local IP it finds first, which usually isn't your Tailscale IP —
# pin it explicitly so Expo Go (wherever it's connecting from) is told the
# right address:
# EXPO_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=100.x.y.z
#
# Setting the above is usually *all* you need: config.js falls back to
# Metro's own reported address for the backend too, so the app will find the
# backend at the same host automatically when both run on this machine.

# --- Backend on a *different* machine than the one running `expo start` ---
# Only needed if the backend (../server.js) is NOT on this same machine —
# e.g. you're running `expo start` on your dev laptop but the backend lives
# on the dedicated server elsewhere:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_HOST=100.x.y.z
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=4173

# --- Backend deployed to the cloud (see ../render/) ---
# A full base URL, for when the backend isn't plain http://host:port —
# takes precedence over the two settings above:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-app.onrender.com
#
# Must match the BASIC_AUTH_USER/BASIC_AUTH_PASS set on that server. React
# Native can't show a password prompt like a browser does, so the app has to
# send these itself. Leave unset for private/LAN setups with no auth.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BASIC_AUTH_USER=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BASIC_AUTH_PASS=
